    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Created on 1 May 1707 by the union of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#england">England</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#scotland">Scotland</a>, with one Parliament at Westminster but separate Scottish law and church.</li><li>Naval power, public credit and trade made it the leading colonial power after the Seven Years’ War ended in 1763.</li><li>It lost the American colonies in 1783 but began the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#industrial-revolution">Industrial Revolution</a>, and it merged with Ireland on 1 January 1801.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#scotland">Scotland</a>’s acceptance of the union was eased by the ‘Equivalent’, a payment of about £398,000 that partly compensated investors in the failed Darien colony in Panama.</p></aside>
    </section>

